==================================================
NICHE ENGINE
==================================================

Create a niche classification system.

A niche can be represented by:

- YouTube category
- keywords
- channel topic
- title semantics
- description semantics
- tags when available
- recurring topic clusters

Do NOT depend exclusively on YouTube's category.

A channel classified as "Entertainment" may actually belong to:

- relationship stories
- luxury lifestyle
- AI storytelling
- celebrity news
- automotive
- comedy
- horror
- documentary
- motivation

Create a flexible taxonomy.

Allow hierarchical niches:

Entertainment
  └── Storytelling
      └── Relationship Stories
          └── Billionaire Romance

==================================================
NICHE SATURATION
==================================================

Implement a Niche Saturation Score.

The score should consider:

- number of active channels
- number of active videos
- upload frequency
- new channels entering the niche
- median views
- percentage of breakout videos
- concentration of views
- number of dominant channels
- recent growth
- competition density

Return:

LOW
MEDIUM
HIGH
VERY HIGH

and also a numeric score from 0-100.

Important:

High competition does not automatically mean a bad niche.

A niche can have:

High demand
High competition
High opportunity

Therefore keep separate concepts:

Demand Score
Competition Score
Opportunity Score

==================================================
OPPORTUNITY SCORE
==================================================

Create a proprietary but transparent Opportunity Score.

Do not pretend it is an official YouTube metric.

Example:

Opportunity Score =
Demand
+ Growth
+ Outlier Frequency
+ Freshness
+ Monetization Potential
- Competition
- Saturation

Normalize to 0-100.

Show users the components.

Example:

Opportunity Score: 87

Demand: 91
Growth: 94
Outlier Potential: 89
Freshness: 92
Competition: 48
Saturation: 41
Monetization: 76

The exact weighting should be configurable in one central configuration file.

